MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A couple quick thoughts without actually looking at what you've checked in.

- Is a vector the most appropriate datatype for an individual chain?  Presumably this will be growing dynamically and requiring contiguous memory and periodic copying of larger and larger chunks of memory seems like a bad idea.  Maybe a deque or a list?

- One place where ragged chains may come up is parallelization across a cluster.  Some nodes of a cluster may be more heavily loaded, have different hardware, etc.  While less likely, this can also happen with threading depending on how consistent and fair the OS scheduler is.

- How will memory requirements scale with large numbers of iterations/parameters/chains for the computations?

- With grouping by individial parameters (instead of grouping by samples) how will fetching multivariate parameters work?  E.g., how do I get back samples of a coviariance matrix?  It seems strangely complicated to have to get back samples of each entry separately.

Cheers,
Marcus

