Thanks for letting me know about the CC_TYPE problem. I've pushed a
fix for that.

I'm glad it's building and linking in parallel. I don't think make
will try running in parallel. All the tests are run through the
test-models target in a for loop. test-models is a phony target, which
means that it runs the for loop every time it is called.

We had the tests run at the same time as it compiled, which would
allow for parallel execution. Unfortunately, that caused make to run
each test twice.

