This is mostly directed at Matt. Hopefully this will help us find out
where the problems are with NUTS II.

We have been timing the runs of the models through Jenkins. The graph
over time for each of the models to run two instances of 2000
iterations each is located here:
http://d1m1s1b1.stat.columbia.edu:8080/job/Stan%20Model%20Tests/139/performance/?

The models that take longer with the current implementation of NUTS II include:
blocker
bones
epil
normal_mixture

Dyes runs faster.

